{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"6255278059f29263363eb3bff8014508524abbb3badc36933189173a35ed3db5","packTokens":6631,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":6354,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and self-service password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user is on the sign-in page when the user submits an email address and password then the screen displays the returned sign-in result or error message\",\n    \"Given A user is on the password-reset page when the user submits an account email address then the screen displays the returned password-reset confirmation or error message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A System Administrator is viewing account management when the administrator opens an account or submits account or access changes then the screen displays account fields and the returned status or error message\",\n    \"Given A user without the System Administrator role opens account management when the page loads then the screen displays an access-denied message or the account-management page is not displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a driver opens today's routes, the Meridian web app shall show only that driver's assigned routes and each route's stops in route order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Route data contains routes assigned to multiple drivers when a driver opens today's route list then the screen lists only routes returned or assigned to that driver and displays each route's stops in order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Before route departure, the Meridian web app shall compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and keep departure blocked until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A route has an expected box that has not been scanned when the driver attempts to complete loading or depart then the screen shows the missing-box status and keeps the departure control unavailable\",\n    \"Given The driver scans a box assigned to another route when the scan is processed then the screen shows a wrong-route warning naming the box and keeps departure blocked\",\n    \"Given Every expected box is scanned and no wrong-route box remains when the driver completes loading then the screen shows loading complete and displays an enabled departure control\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show dispatchers each route stop's status and last-updated time.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The route service returns stop statuses and update-time fields when a dispatcher opens route monitoring then the screen displays each stop's returned status and last-updated time\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show each route box's latest available temperature, status, and alerts from the supplied gateway data and identify cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The gateway feed returns temperature, status, and alert data for route boxes when the driver opens route monitoring then the screen displays each box's current temperature, status, and returned alerts\",\n    \"Given The browser is disconnected and cached temperature data is available when the driver opens box monitoring then the screen displays the cached temperature value and marks it stale\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When scanned stock is On Hold, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason and prevent handover of that box.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A stop includes a scanned box whose returned stock status is On Hold when the driver opens that box's handover controls then the screen displays “Do not deliver” and the hold reason and offers no enabled handover control for that box\",\n    \"Given A stop includes both On Hold and deliverable boxes when the driver opens the handover screen then the screen permits handover only for deliverable boxes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When online, if a scanned box is reported as Recalled, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of that box.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A driver is online and the service reports a scanned box as Recalled when the driver opens that box's handover controls then the screen displays “Do not deliver” and no enabled handover control for that box\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record an eligible handover with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A box is eligible for handover when the driver enters the receiver name, captures a signature and photo, and completes handover then the handover request contains the receiver, signature, photo, actual completion time, and available location fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If browser location is denied or unavailable, the Meridian web app shall allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Browser location access is denied or unavailable when the driver completes an otherwise eligible handover then the screen displays the completed handover and a location-unavailable value, and the request records location as unavailable\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record full or partial refusal only by whole box and require a reason for each refused box.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A driver is recording a refusal when the driver selects refused boxes and submits a reason for each then the screen displays each refused whole box with its reason and offers no partial-box quantity control\",\n    \"Given The service returns a refusal and quarantine result when the driver opens the completed refusal then the screen displays the returned refusal status and quarantine status for each refused box\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While offline, the Meridian web app shall retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally and automatically send queued work when connectivity returns, preserving the handover's occurrence time and reusing the same handover identifier on retries.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The browser is offline when the driver records loading, handover, or refusal work then the screen shows each action in the pending queue and retains its entered values\",\n    \"Given Queued work exists and connectivity returns when the web app reconnects then the screen shows queued work being sent without requiring resubmission, and displays the returned sync status\",\n    \"Given A handover was recorded offline when the web app sends it or retries an interrupted send then the request contains the original handover time and the same handover identifier as the original request\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, the Meridian web app shall show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The route returned after reconnection differs and unsent work exists when the driver reconnects and the app reconciles the route then the screen lists route differences and affected boxes requiring review\",\n    \"Given Route differences have unresolved affected boxes when the driver attempts to continue route work then the screen blocks continuing and shows the unresolved boxes\",\n    \"Given A handover was completed offline before the route changed when the new route is synchronized then the screen still displays the completed handover and its original time\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, the Meridian web app shall retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An offline handover is synchronized and the service returns a hold or recall conflict and quality-case result when the driver or quality user opens the synchronized record then the screen displays the retained handover, conflict flag, and returned quality-case status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the returned recommendation, using the configured tier rules.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An excursion review receives temperature history, tier budgets, and a recommendation when a Quality reviewer opens the affected handling unit then the screen displays the full history, used and remaining allowance for each tier, and the recommendation\",\n    \"Given Configured tier limits and allowances are returned for different products when a user views settings or excursion reviews for those products then the screen displays the same configured tier-limit and allowance values for each product\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall present a single-person quality-decision flow only for an excursion within the first tier above or below the permitted band with allowance remaining, and otherwise present a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager; written justification is required when a decision opposes the recommendation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An excursion is within the first tier above or below the band and has allowance remaining when an eligible Quality Officer opens the decision form then the screen displays the single-person decision controls\",\n    \"Given An excursion is outside the single-person case or has no allowance remaining when a Quality Officer opens the decision form then the screen requires a proposal and separate Quality Manager approval\",\n    \"Given The proposing Quality Officer also has the Quality Manager role when that person attempts to approve the proposal then the screen does not offer an approval action to that same person\",\n    \"Given A proposed decision opposes the displayed recommendation when a user prepares the decision then the screen requires both decision participants and a written-justification field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall require identity confirmation using the account's sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision, and present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user is ready to sign a quality decision when the user submits the signing form then the screen requires identity confirmation and a reason before showing the signed-decision status\",\n    \"Given A decision is returned as signed when a user opens that decision then the screen shows signed values as read-only, provides a separate superseding-decision action, and offers no edit or delete control\",\n    \"Given The service returns an earlier signed decision and a superseding decision when a reviewer opens decision history then the screen displays both signed decision records and identifies the superseding decision\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the service returns a quality disposition, the Meridian web app shall show resulting stock, order, and route status and the earlier and current disposition when superseded.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns a release, rejection, or superseding disposition when a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit then the screen displays the returned stock, order, and route status and disposition history\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock and prevent entry of quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user opens destruction entry for rejected stock when the user records destruction then the request contains destruction date, quantity, and witness fields\",\n    \"Given The entered destruction quantity exceeds the displayed rejected quantity when the user submits the entry then the screen shows a validation error and sends no destruction request\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall identify quality decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager's waiting-decisions view.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns a decision waiting more than four hours as escalated when a Quality Manager opens waiting decisions then the screen lists the decision and displays its escalated status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions, collecting product, one or more lots, reason, and severity for recall start, and display each returned action result.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Quality Manager opens recall start when the manager enters product, lot numbers, reason, severity, and signature then the recall request contains those values and the screen displays the returned recall result\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager closes a recall when the manager submits the signed close action then the close request contains the signature and the screen displays the returned close status or error message\",\n    \"Given A user who is not identified as eligible to manage recalls opens recall management when recall actions load then the screen does not display recall start or close actions\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A recall trace response contains affected locations and delivery records when a Quality Manager opens the trace then the screen displays each returned warehouse, box, route, customer delivery, quantity, delivery date, and receiver\",\n    \"Given The service returns trace quantities and the lot's total received quantity when the user views the trace summary then the screen displays the returned trace total alongside the received quantity\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns an active recall notice for the signed-in customer's organisation when the customer opens the portal then the screen displays the recall notice, its returned status, affected deliveries, and a response entry point\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let customers submit per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities, allow a total below the delivered amount as unaccounted, and reject a total above it.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A customer opens a recall response for a delivery when the customer enters on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities then the response request contains the entered quantity fields for that delivery\",\n    \"Given The reported quantities total less than the delivered quantity when the customer submits the response then the screen accepts the values and displays the difference as unaccounted quantity\",\n    \"Given The reported quantities exceed the delivered quantity when the customer submits the response then the screen displays a validation error or returned error message and sends no invalid response request\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, identify outstanding customers and reminder status when supplied, and let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns recall progress and outstanding customers when a Quality Manager opens recall progress then the screen displays the accounted percentage and outstanding-customer list\",\n    \"Given The service returns customer response and reminder statuses when a user opens recall progress then the screen displays the returned reminder status\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager selects unaccounted quantity for write-off when the manager submits the write-off then the request contains a signed justification and the screen displays the returned write-off status or refusal message\",\n    \"Given A recall has unaccounted quantity without a signed write-off when a Quality Manager attempts to close the recall then the screen blocks submission and displays the outstanding quantity or returned close error\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show customers only their organisation's current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns orders and delivery data for a customer's organisation and other organisations when the customer opens the orders page then the screen lists only that organisation's orders and displays returned status, lots, and expiry dates\",\n    \"Given The service returns an in-transit delivery with arrival and temperature status when the customer views the delivery then the screen displays planned arrival and in-range or out-of-range status and no other customer's identity or delivery details\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery with products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A completed delivery has a certificate available when the customer selects certificate download then the downloaded file is a PDF containing the listed delivery, handover, temperature, excursion, and decision fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When late readings produce a new certificate version, the Meridian web app shall list the new and earlier versions and keep each available for download.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns a new certificate version and retains the earlier version when the customer opens certificate history then the screen lists both versions and provides a file download link for each\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall present the customer portal and certificates in the user's selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account's configured time zone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The user selects Arabic when the portal and a delivery certificate are displayed then the screen and certificate display Arabic content with right-to-left direction for tables and charts\",\n    \"Given The user's account has a configured time zone when the portal displays order or delivery dates and times then the screen displays the values in that configured time zone\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason, with filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Audit entries are returned for multiple records, users, dates, and action types when an Auditor opens the audit trail then the screen displays each entry's actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason\",\n    \"Given An Auditor selects audit filters when the filters are applied and the Auditor exports the view then the screen displays the matching returned list and provides a file containing the filtered view\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot-history response contains receipt, movement, delivery, or destruction events when an Auditor opens lot history then the screen displays the returned events in time order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed report figures, including the specified excursion, refusal/destruction, delivery, decision-time, expiry, and recall measures.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns report figures for selected date range and warehouse when staff open the reports screen then the screen displays every specified report measure and its returned value\",\n    \"Given A staff user has warehouse access scope when the user filters reports and exports them then the screen offers only in-scope warehouses and the downloaded CSV file contains the displayed filtered figures\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authorized staff user opens opening-inventory entry when the user enters lot and stock details then the request contains the entered opening lot and stock fields and the screen displays the returned result or error\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A delivery record within its retention period includes signature and photo evidence when an authorized user opens the delivery record then the screen displays the signature and photo fields or their available file links\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n  \"The Meridian web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n  \"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.\",\n  \"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}